@startuml
title The four guard surfaces and what each builds

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #374151
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.3
skinparam component {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
}
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
}

' ── The surfaces a language author writes (left) ────────────────────────
rectangle "Guard surfaces in language!" as Surf #DBEAFE {
  component "guards { } block\n(parse_guards)" as G #BFDBFE
  component "?guard:Guard slot\n(parse_term_param)" as Slot #BFDBFE
  component "where-clause sublanguage\n(predicate_pratt.rs)" as Where #BFDBFE
  component "logic { relation } block\n(parse_logic)" as Logic #BFDBFE
  component "#[tier(...)] directive\n(parse_tier_directive)" as Tier #BFDBFE
}

' ── What each surface builds (right) ────────────────────────────────────
rectangle "What each builds" as Built #DCFCE7 {
  component "GuardConfig\n(channels / theories / connectives)" as GC #BBF7D0
  component "TermParam::GuardBody\n+ per-instance BehavioralPred" as TP #BBF7D0
  component "BehavioralPred\n(RelationQuery / Quantified /\nAnd / Or / Not / Implies)" as BP #BBF7D0
  component "external relations\n(LogicBlock)" as Rel #BBF7D0
  component "TierDirective\n(tier, bound, force)" as TD #BBF7D0
}

G    --> GC : builds
Slot --> TP : builds
Where --> BP : builds
Logic --> Rel : builds
Tier --> TD : builds

note bottom of Where
  The where-clause text is parsed by prattail's PredicateParser;
  where is NOT a reserved keyword — it is a literal sitting before
  the ?guard:Guard slot, which lowers to a GuardExpression parser
  item and switches into the predicate sublanguage. Any literal could
  precede the slot.
end note

note bottom of Built #FEF3C7
  Beyond these authorable surfaces, the OSLF substrate algebras are now wired into
  the live pipeline as default-off lints (RT03 / RT07 / LP01 / HM01, the N06-ISO
  bisimulation supersede, the letprop→PATA decision) — see the substrate
  wiring-status map. Wired is not writable: those still have no language! surface.
end note

legend right
|= Color |= Side |
|<#DBEAFE> | guard surface (what the author writes) |
|<#DCFCE7> | the obligation / config it builds |
|<#FEF3C7> | algebra wired as a default-off lint (not an authorable surface) |
endlegend
@enduml
